From: Genesi OS Team <dev@genesios.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Make slider grooves white

Darkly renders the inactive part of a slider from WindowText at 30% opacity.
On Genesi's translucent dark surfaces that blends into the application body
and makes the control hard to locate. Keep the groove explicitly white while
leaving the active section on the normal highlight colour.
---
 kstyle/darklystyle.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kstyle/darklystyle.cpp b/kstyle/darklystyle.cpp
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/kstyle/darklystyle.cpp
+++ b/kstyle/darklystyle.cpp
@@ -8169,7 +8169,7 @@ void Style::drawComplexControl(ComplexControl control, const QStyleOption *optio
         auto grooveRect(subControlRect(CC_Slider, sliderOption, SC_SliderGroove, widget));

         // base color
-        const auto grooveColor(_helper->alphaColor(palette.color(QPalette::WindowText), 0.3));
+        const QColor grooveColor(Qt::white);

         if (!enabled)
             _helper->renderSliderGroove(painter, grooveRect, grooveColor);
--
